# PreToolUse safety rules: block dangerous Bash commands
# Format: id@@regex@@message (delimiter: @@)
# Each line's regex is checked against the command string via grep -E.
# Matched commands are blocked (exit 2) with the given message.
# Lines starting with # are comments. Empty lines are skipped.
git-push-force@@git\s+push\s+.*--force(\s|$)@@git push --force is not allowed. Use --force-with-lease if necessary.
git-push-f@@git\s+push\s+.*-f(\s|$)@@git push -f is not allowed. Use --force-with-lease if necessary.
git-checkout-dot@@git\s+checkout\s+\.\s*$@@git checkout . discards all changes. Use git stash or commit first.
git-reset-hard@@git\s+reset\s+--hard@@git reset --hard is destructive. Stash or commit changes first.
git-clean-f@@git\s+clean\s+-f@@git clean -f permanently deletes untracked files. Review with git clean -n first.
rm-rf-dangerous@@rm\s+-rf\s+(/|\.\.|~)@@rm -rf on root, parent, or home directory is not allowed.
package-publish@@(npm\s+publish|cargo\s+publish|twine\s+upload|gem\s+push|pod\s+trunk\s+push)@@Package publishing requires manual execution outside Claude Code.
db-destructive@@(DROP\s+(TABLE|DATABASE)|TRUNCATE\s+TABLE)@@Destructive database operations. Run manually with review.
mass-kill@@(kill\s+-9\s+-1|killall\s|pkill\s+-9)@@Mass process killing is not allowed.
